From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: an elevated program that is the person keeps the person's Start menu and desktop

0617 gave every program the elevation broker started the all-users Programs, Start menu, Startup and
desktop: it ran with the SYSTEM account's token, whose own folders nobody sees. Since 7601 an
elevated program is the person who asked (their SID, HKCU and profile), and on Windows an elevated
per-user install keeps that person's Start menu and desktop. Mixxx's per-user MSI, installed
through the consent prompt, put its shortcuts in all users' Start menu. The mapping now applies only
when the program's token really is the SYSTEM account's. Installs for all users still go to all
users: ALLUSERS=1 (0590 points msi's folders there), Inno's /ALLUSERS and NSIS's SetShellVarContext
all ask for the common folders themselves.

The Apps & features entry of a per-user MSI stays under HKLM: Windows Installer writes it there too
(for the installing user's view only).

David 2026-11-23. Gate test-elevfolders (now with the SYSTEM account of a shared prefix); mutant
SG_MUTANT_ELEVATED_ALWAYS_COMMON.
---
--- a/dlls/shell32/shellpath.c
+++ b/dlls/shell32/shellpath.c
@@ -2897,6 +2897,20 @@
 /*************************************************************************
  * SHGetFolderPathAndSubDirW		[SHELL32.@]
  */
+/* Stained Glass OS 9004: is this thread's token the SYSTEM account's? */
+static BOOL sg_token_is_system(void)
+{
+    BYTE buf[SECURITY_MAX_SID_SIZE + sizeof(TOKEN_USER)];
+    TOKEN_USER *user = (TOKEN_USER *)buf;
+    DWORD size;
+
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_ELEVATED_ALWAYS_COMMON
+    return TRUE;
+#endif
+    if (!GetTokenInformation( GetCurrentThreadEffectiveToken(), TokenUser, buf, sizeof(buf), &size )) return FALSE;
+    return IsWellKnownSid( user->User.Sid, WinLocalSystemSid );
+}
+
 HRESULT WINAPI SHGetFolderPathAndSubDirW(
 	HWND hwndOwner,    /* [I] owner window */
 	int nFolder,       /* [I] CSIDL identifying the folder */
@@ -2929,7 +2943,12 @@
      * An installer's shortcuts went there (Blender, Temurin, Audacity,
      * Winamp: not in Start). Its Start menu, programs, startup and desktop
      * are the ones all users share. */
-    if (!hToken && GetEnvironmentVariableW( L"SG_IN_BROKER", NULL, 0 ))
+    /* Stained Glass OS 9004: only when that program really is the SYSTEM account. Since 7601 an
+     * elevated program is the person who asked (their SID, HKCU and profile), as on Windows, where an
+     * elevated per-user install keeps the person's Start menu and desktop: Mixxx's per-user MSI put
+     * its shortcuts in all users' Start menu. An install for all users says so itself (ALLUSERS=1:
+     * 0590; Inno's /ALLUSERS and NSIS's SetShellVarContext all ask for the common folders). */
+    if (!hToken && GetEnvironmentVariableW( L"SG_IN_BROKER", NULL, 0 ) && sg_token_is_system())
     {
         static const BYTE common[][2] =
         {
